&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Integrity and Attestation team&#39;s remit is to prove what is running at Anthropic: what code it is, where it came from, and whether the machine underneath it is in a known-good state. We build the systems that cryptographically verify build artifacts, model weights, and machines, from hardware roots of trust through firmware and boot to the credentials a workload receives. We also secure the management plane of our servers. These controls protect our model weights and customer data across cloud providers and bare-metal AI data centers, including sites operated by partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring an Engineering Manager to lead this team. Anthropic is bringing up new compute quickly, across new hardware platforms and new partners, and each one has to meet the same bar. In this role you will set the team&#39;s charter, practices, and priorities. You will partner with our infrastructure, data center, and hardware teams, as well as outside vendors, so that integrity is designed in rather than added later. The goal is simple to state: a machine gets secrets and workloads only after it proves it should, and a new site reaches that bar without slowing down compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the integrity roadmap: threat model from silicon and firmware up through the operating system and workloads, decide what to build, and deliver it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be able to reason about the design and implementation of remote attestation, measured and verified boot, hardware roots of trust (TPM, SPDM), machine identity, and the reference values that define known-good&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make attestation the default path, so machines receive credentials and join clusters only after proving their firmware, system software, and security configuration, with no human in the loop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build provenance for what we deploy: signed build artifacts and model weights, independent verification, and tamper-evident transparency logs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the protection of sensitive data in use and at rest, including encryption and the chokepoints that control access to it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure the server management plane across every site: scoped and audited access to baseboard management controllers and management of per-device credentials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make security repeatable as compute grows, so a new site or hardware platform inherits these controls in hours, not weeks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join compute bring-up, data center, and hardware teams at design time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define clear ownership with partner teams: when operations move to another team, your team keeps the security properties and can prove they still hold&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the integrity evidence for our security goals and compliance: the invariants hold, and you can prove it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, grow, and retain senior security software engineers; own their career development, and set the practices the team runs on as it scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low ego, high empathy; has built diverse teams and has former reports who would vouch for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing infrastructure or security engineering teams, including hiring, developing, and managing senior and staff engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has grown engineers into staff or lead roles, and experience with performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Created and maintained a high performing in hypergrowth environments. Kept a team intact and delivering through reorgs, charter changes, or leadership turnover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a security or infrastructure domain end to end: setting multi-year strategy, delivering year-long cross-organizational work with little direction, and answering to executives for its risk and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An appreciation for distributed systems and properties beyond security, including reliability, efficiency, and maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaled a team and its systems together through hypergrowth, where last quarter&#39;s architecture was already too small&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on engineering in at least one of: platform security, secure boot and firmware, hardware roots of trust, confidential computing, or software supply chain integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Threat modeling and risk assessment for systems that span hardware and software, with strong security judgment and pragmatism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable leading through ambiguity with multiple partner teams and outside vendors, where you don&#39;t control the hardware or the schedule&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5+ years managing engineering teams and 8+ years hands-on in platform, infrastructure, or security engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built or operated remote attestation, device identity, or fleet-wide boot integrity at production scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked with BMCs, Redfish, GPU or accelerator attestation, or large-scale bare-metal provisioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Nitro, SEV-SNP, TDX, or similar confidential computing platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built signing, provenance, or transparency systems such as Sigstore, SLSA, or binary transparency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designed key management or offline ceremonies for high-value secrets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked in high-assurance environments where controls had to be evidenced, not just deployed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taken infrastructure from zero to one and then to maturity: built the first version where nothing existed, then run and hardened it into a system other teams depend on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built or rebuilt a hiring loop and held the bar while adding headcount quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pragmatic and steady: cares about unblocking research, product and compute as much as a clean architecture, and brings patience and judgment to opinionated senior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive communicator in writing and in person&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI security and safety concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$405,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$405,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Next.js team builds the open source framework that powers millions of applications and shapes how developers build for the web. Our work sits at the intersection of React, framework architecture, developer experience, infrastructure, performance, and production reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Engineering Team Lead to help build and lead a team working on Next.js. This is a hands-on player/coach role for an experienced engineer who wants to remain close to the code while helping a small team do its best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be an engineer first and a manager second. You will contribute directly to the framework, lead major technical initiatives, review code, debug complex production issues, and help make architectural decisions. You will also support the engineers around you through clear direction, thoughtful feedback, and practical coaching.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional people management role. You will spend the majority of your time on technical leadership and engineering execution. You should be comfortable owning difficult parts of the codebase while creating enough context and clarity for others to move quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Product, Design, and engineers across Vercel to guide the evolution of Next.js across rendering, caching, routing, build systems, and developer tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and ship Next.js:&lt;/strong&gt; Write production code, review pull requests, debug difficult issues, and contribute directly to the framework and its supporting systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead major technical initiatives:&lt;/strong&gt; Take ownership of complex projects from initial exploration through architecture, implementation, rollout, and production follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set technical direction:&lt;/strong&gt; Make sound architectural decisions across rendering, caching, routing, build systems, runtime behavior, and developer tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay close to real problems:&lt;/strong&gt; Investigate performance regressions, production failures, and developer pain points. Turn what you learn into practical improvements to the framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the engineering bar:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish strong patterns for code quality, testing, performance, reliability, observability, and incremental delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coach through the work:&lt;/strong&gt; Help engineers grow through pairing, design reviews, code reviews, technical feedback, and shared ownership of challenging problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide focused people leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Set clear expectations, give candid feedback, support career development, and help maintain a high-trust and accountable team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve team execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Create lightweight planning and decision-making practices that clarify ownership, reduce unnecessary coordination, and help the team ship consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across Vercel:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with Product, Design, Infrastructure, Developer Experience, and other engineering teams so framework changes integrate cleanly across the Vercel platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion open source:&lt;/strong&gt; Work in public, engage thoughtfully with contributors, and balance community needs with the team’s product and technical priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help grow the team:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in recruiting, assess technical talent, and help new engineers become productive in a complex codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of software engineering experience and remain highly effective as a hands-on engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have led engineers or small technical teams, whether as a team lead, tech lead, staff engineer, engineering manager, or founder.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have recent experience writing, reviewing, and shipping production code. You are not looking to step away from engineering execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong technical judgment across React, framework architecture, or the systems behind a large-scale open source project, including rendering, caching, routing, build tooling, and runtime behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can take a complex technical problem, form a clear point of view, write the critical code, and bring other engineers along with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know when to lead from the front and when to create space for someone else to take ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building products or infrastructure for developers and understand the quality, performance, stability, and usability standards this audience expects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think in systems and can guide a team toward clean abstractions, consistent framework patterns, and technical decisions that hold up at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working through ambiguity and solving problems from first principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You balance speed and quality. You favor incremental delivery and real-world feedback while recognizing when foundational infrastructure requires deeper investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly in writing, facilitate productive technical debate, and make decisions when a path forward is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use AI tools in your own workflow and have informed opinions about how agentic products should work for developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining or contributing to a major open source project, particularly in the React or Next.js ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with compilers, bundlers, caching, rendering systems, or distributed infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a small, senior engineering team while continuing to make substantial individual contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience forming a team or technical direction from zero to one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Next.js codebase, though this is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusive healthcare package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and growth support, including mentorship and opportunities to attend events that build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible time off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The equipment you need to do your role, plus a work-from-home budget to outfit your space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $230,000 to $340,000. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program, depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclosures:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vercel.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Job Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; for more information on how we handle your data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Vercel is committed to fostering and empowering an inclusive community within our organization. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Vercel encourages everyone to apply for our available positions, even if they don&#39;t necessarily check every box on the job description.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Head of Professional Services to build and lead Vercel&#39;s global professional services organization, composed of our Technical Account Management (TAM) and Forward Deployed Engineering (FDE) functions. These functions embed directly with our most strategic customers to design, build, and ship production applications on Vercel using Vercel&#39;s core platform, Next.js and our agent stack, taking projects from first prototype through production rollout. You will define how this function operates: the engagement model, the delivery methodology, the commercial structure, and the team itself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report directly to our Global Head of Field Engineering, and partner closely with GTM and Product Leadership to run a business function that turns our largest customers&#39; complex implementations into production deployments, drives adoption and expansion, and feeds what you learn in the field back into our product roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid position based in San Francisco, Austin or New York, with 3 days per week (Monday, Tuesday, Friday) required in office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the engagement model: how engagements are scoped, staffed, sequenced, and measured, and which accounts qualify for embedded support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery excellence for strategic customer engagements, from discovery and technical scoping through production deployment and stabilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the commercial model for professional services, including packaging, pricing, capacity planning, and resource allocation across competing customer priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay hands-on where it matters: architecture reviews, system design, and unblocking critical engagements alongside your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Codify field learnings into repeatable playbooks, reference architectures, and delivery patterns that scale beyond individual engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you need&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in software engineering, forward deployed engineering, or technical consulting roles, with at least 5 years leading customer-facing engineering or delivery teams in a high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a team, function, or service line from zero, including hiring, methodology, and operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in modern web technologies (JavaScript/TypeScript, React, Next.js, Node.js, cloud infrastructure) with the ability to review code and whiteboard architectures credibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or deploying LLM-powered applications and an understanding of how model behavior shapes product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial acumen: you have scoped, priced, and delivered technical engagements for enterprise customers and understand utilization, margin, and capacity tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus if you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built with Vercel, Next.js, AI SDK, or v0.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have led forward deployed or embedded engineering teams at an AI-native or developer platform company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have owned a professional services P&amp;amp;L or defined services pricing and packaging from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable representing the function externally at conferences, customer executive briefings, or large-scale events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Compensation:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The San Francisco, CA base pay range for this role is $300,000 - $370,000 plus annual bonus. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
